+# Mobile staff-support requests
+
+Phase 9 follows backend 42b4552 plus the v4, claims, notifications, SMS and biometric mobile patches. Apply mobile-support.patch last. No migration, dependency or staff frontend change is required.
+
+| Route under /api/v1/mobile | Use |
+| --- | --- |
+| GET /beneficiaries/me/support?page=1&pageSize=20 | Own retained request summaries and pagination |
+| POST /beneficiaries/me/support | Create with requestId (UUID retry identifier), language (en/bs), messageText |
+| GET /beneficiaries/me/support/:requestId | Own request metadata and saved messages |
+| POST /beneficiaries/me/support/:requestId/messages | Follow up with messageId (UUID retry identifier) and messageText |
+
+These routes require the beneficiary mobile session. They create linked ESCALATED chatbot sessions using HUMAN_REQUESTED and an initial USER message marked MOBILE_SUPPORT_REQUEST. The generic chatbot bearer credential remains null, so anonymous chatbot token routes cannot read them. Queries require the signed-in owner, the source marker and unexpired retention. Mobile bodies cannot set beneficiary, staff, sender, assignment or status. Existing staff queue scope, reply ownership and resolution controls remain authoritative. The staff Help cases / Help conversations workspace at /help-cases sees the request in its Escalation inbox after refresh; a same-barangay facilitator or authorized global staff can respond. Existing linked cases cannot be reassigned through anonymous referral.
+
+English/Bisaya en/bs maps to staff en/ceb in storage. Message text is retained in its submitted language; staff replies are displayed as written. The existing plain-text 1000-character validation and credential redactor are reused. Responses omit staff identifiers, scores, raw generic credentials and database fields. Audit entries retain actor/reference and omit message contents. No external AI, SMS/email, automated staff reply or personal-record lookup is invoked by this support feature.
+
+Create/reply retries reuse client UUIDs. They are correlation identifiers, not authorization credentials. Transactions lock/revalidate the mobile account/session and use Serializable isolation, mapping conflicts to 409. Replaying the same normalized message returns the saved thread, including after resolution; changing a replay's content returns 409. New replies require an open escalation, the existing chatbot response window and space under its message cap. GET returns at most the existing hard maximum of 500 messages. Retention and reply duration use the existing chatbot configuration; expired retention hides the request, and resolution or an ended response window disables new mobile replies. The beneficiary may then create another request.
+
+Updates use manual refresh. This patch does not publish new mobile lifecycle events or add polling, realtime transport, staff notifications, push, response-time guarantees or attachments. Staff refreshes the existing queue; mobile refreshes requests/conversation. No public generic-chatbot behavior or staff permissions are changed.
+
+Verification: mobile npm.cmd run test:shared runs sequentially on isolated PostgreSQL 51244. The support case exercises the real TypeScript client and Express API, creation and retries, language mapping, scoped staff queue/replies/resolution, duplicate prevention, protected fields, public-token rejection, cross-owner/other-barangay rejection, retention, pagination and logout. Fixtures are synthetic and removed afterward; no real staff message is sent during development checks. Default backend tests run separately with npm test.
